{"files": [{"id": 39621146, "name": "ppat.1011232.s012.tif", "size": 1699616, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/39621146", "supplied_md5": "88119195a9e44920b0cbc738ff67314b", "computed_md5": "88119195a9e44920b0cbc738ff67314b", "mimetype": "image/tiff"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 139140, "full_name": "Tian Xia", "first_name": "Tian", "last_name": "Xia", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 10164, "full_name": "Xin Wu", "first_name": "Xin", "last_name": "Wu", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Xin_Wu", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797226, "full_name": "Eunjin Hong", "first_name": "Eunjin", "last_name": "Hong", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797229, "full_name": "Kyle Jung", "first_name": "Kyle", "last_name": "Jung", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797232, "full_name": "Chih-Jen Lai", "first_name": "Chih-Jen", "last_name": "Lai", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797235, "full_name": "Mi-Jeong Kwak", "first_name": "Mi-Jeong", "last_name": "Kwak", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797238, "full_name": "Hogyu Seo", "first_name": "Hogyu", "last_name": "Seo", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 2560966, "full_name": "Stephanie Kim", "first_name": "Stephanie", "last_name": "Kim", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 583925, "full_name": "Zhongyi Jiang", "first_name": "Zhongyi", "last_name": "Jiang", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797241, "full_name": "Inho Cha", "first_name": "Inho", "last_name": "Cha", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 9611629, "full_name": "Jae U. Jung", "first_name": "Jae U.", "last_name": "Jung", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Role_of_glycosphingolipid_biosynthesis_pathway_in_HRTV_and_DBV_entry_/22278524", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>Sphingolipid <i>de novo</i> synthesis pathway is initiated in the ER, where palmitoyl-CoA and serine are catalyzed into ceramide by enzymes, including SPT and CerS. Subsequently, ceramide is converted to GalCer by UGT8 in the ER or directly transported to the Golgi complex. In the Golgi complex, ceramide is further converted into GlcCer by UGCG. GlcCer is then converted to other complex GSLs by adding variable carbohydrate groups. GlcCer and GSLs are delivered to the plasma membrane by vesicular transport and GlcCer in the plasma membrane is subsequently recycled from cell surface and degraded in the lysosome <i>via</i> the endocytic pathway. HRTV infection is triggered by an interaction between viral glycoproteins and host receptor(s) on cell surface. Virus particles are then internalized and enter early endosomes. During viral trafficking, endosome fuses with lysosome, inducing the disassociation of Gn/Gc dimer and the conformational change of Gc protein. Subsequently, Gc protein inserts into target membrane and interacts with GlcCer to form a stable protein-lipid complex, which is essential for an efficient membrane fusion for viral genome releases its genome to the cytosol. 3-KDS, 3-ketodihydrosphingosine; Cer, ceramide; CerS, ceramide synthase; ER, endoplasmic reticulum; GalCer, galactosylceramide; GlcCer, glucosylceramide; GSL, glycosphingolipid; SPT, serine palmitoyltransferase; UGCG, ceramide Glucosyltransferase; UGT8, uridine diphosphate glycosyltransferase 8. Figure created with <a href=\"http://BioRender.com\" target=\"_blank\">BioRender.com</a>.</p> <p>(TIF)</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 1699616, "created_date": "2023-03-15T17:35:08Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-10T08:57:44Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["recombinant viruses pseudotyped", "potential therapeutic target", "group binding pocket", "glucose ceramide glucosyltransferase", "dabie bandavirus glycoprotein", "dabie bandavirus </", "borne zoonotic viruses", "early entry events", "glycosphingolipid biosynthesis pathway", "biophysical analyses showed", "dangerous viral pathogens", "recovered viral entry", "produces glccer resulted", "play essential roles", "heartland bandavirus </", "div >< p", "mediated membrane fusion", "galcer ), glucosylceramide", "viral entry", "viral fusion", "mutagenesis showed", "glccer glycosphingolipid", "viral lifecycle", "membrane structure", "membrane lipids", "wide crispr", "stable protein", "largely unknown", "large expansion", "laccer ),", "high fatality", "hemorrhagic fever", "glccer targeted", "glccer interaction", "exogenous supplement", "etiologic agents", "emerging tick", "dependent manner", "deficient cells", "d841 residue", "climate changes"], "keywords": ["recombinant viruses pseudotyped", "potential therapeutic target", "group binding pocket", "glucose ceramide glucosyltransferase", "dabie bandavirus glycoprotein", "dabie bandavirus </", "borne zoonotic viruses", "early entry events", "glycosphingolipid biosynthesis pathway", "biophysical analyses showed", "dangerous viral pathogens", "recovered viral entry", "produces glccer resulted", "play essential roles", "heartland bandavirus </", "div >< p", "mediated membrane fusion", "galcer ), glucosylceramide", "viral entry", "viral fusion", "mutagenesis showed", "glccer glycosphingolipid", "viral lifecycle", "membrane structure", "membrane lipids", "wide crispr", "stable protein", "largely unknown", "large expansion", "laccer ),", "high fatality", "hemorrhagic fever", "glccer targeted", "glccer interaction", "exogenous supplement", "etiologic agents", "emerging tick", "dependent manner", "deficient cells", "d841 residue", "climate changes"], "categories": [{"id": 4, "title": "Biochemistry", "parent_id": 38, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 7, "title": "Medicine", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 8, "title": "Microbiology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 13, "title": "Genetics", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 14, "title": "Molecular Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 734, "title": "Biological Sciences not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 132, "title": "Infectious Diseases", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 134, "title": "Virology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}], "references": ["https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1011232"], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "Xia, Tian; Wu, Xin; Hong, Eunjin; Jung, Kyle; Lai, Chih-Jen; Kwak, Mi-Jeong; et al. (2023). Role of glycosphingolipid biosynthesis pathway in HRTV and DBV entry.. PLOS Pathogens. Figure. https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1011232.s012", "related_materials": [{"id": 65943881, "identifier": "10.1371/journal.ppat.1011232", "title": "Glucosylceramide is essential for Heartland and Dabie bandavirus glycoprotein-induced membrane fusion", "relation": "IsSupplementTo", "identifier_type": "DOI", "is_linkout": true, "link": "https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1011232"}], "is_embargoed": false, "embargo_date": null, "embargo_type": null, "embargo_title": "", "embargo_reason": "", "embargo_options": [], "id": 22278524, "title": "Role of glycosphingolipid biosynthesis pathway in HRTV and DBV entry.", "doi": "10.1371/journal.ppat.1011232.s012", "handle": "", "url": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/22278524", "published_date": "2023-03-15T17:35:08Z", "thumb": "https://s3-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com